    narr:narration """Tina Team's profile now runs across three dated movements. The first frames [the four-site rollout and the site nobody wants to touch](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_5), argues [why a double cutover is a different class of problem](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15), and pins [a hard two-week number on the soak](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_17) grounded in [what the spring pilot's exception queue showed](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_19), held as [evidence-first over speed-first](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_22). The second movement inverts it: she opens by [correcting herself at the top rather than burying it](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_1), [retracts the two-week soak outright](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_3), explains [the re-analysis that found the old number was measuring a retired weekly job](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_5) — [a job gone since July, its figure attached to the site as though a property of it](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_7) — proposes [a one-week soak preserving the same margin](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_9) while holding [the sequencing itself doesn't move](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_11), names [defensible over conservatively-for-the-wrong-reason](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_14) as the principle, counts [the three-week programme cost](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_17), notes [the flaw would have surfaced at the first site anyway, and worse](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_24), and commits to [writing it up the same day](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_22). A third, newer thread opens onto legacy-system wind-down: she admits [she'd assumed they'd just keep paying the vendor to leave it running](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_6), probes [how long the archive gets held](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_19), and decides [the retention question belongs in the vendor exit conversation, not after it](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_24). Around the spine runs a facilitator's register — [terse openers and closers](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_2), short acknowledgments ([\"That's the question.\"](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_7), [\"I'm with you on that.\"](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_9)), a blunt reality-check on [nobody deciding off stale counts](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_29), and [easy concession when a proposal lightens site-team load](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_41). A separate child records [a review acceptance act, relayed through Claude's report](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_2) — her signature on a decision, not her own voiced argument.""" ;
